    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:4b5ff9b4a37f43cc",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "77634841de185a6e1d609dc100af0921b6834b51b902b1ac92fb042b3082f3e4",
      "text": "Day 3 · Breakfast and transfer to the airport for your flight to Calama. On arrival, transfer to San Pedro de Atacama for a half-day excursion to the Moon Valley. A few kilometres from San Pedro, among the sharp ridges and strange shapes of the Cordillera de la Sal, the Moon Valley is a true geological spectacle and part of Los Flamencos National Reserve. Spend the afternoon among its extraordinary landscapes, with unbeatable views of the Andes and its volcanoes; at sunset, golden and red tones flood the desert. Enjoy a freshly prepared Pisco Sour as you take in the scenery.\n\nEvening · A special stargazing experience in the desert: the Atacama is one of the world’s top places to see the stars. Our chef serves drinks in the middle of the desert while you gaze through a powerful telescope with a knowledgeable guide. Return to the hotel.",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "word_exact",
        "fileId": "1nHB-5Xavr6R_fNkR408Fk_Ch8G6c2l00",
